{title: 541 - Lord, Speak to Me}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #541 • CANONBURY • L.M.}
{lyricist: Frances Ridley Havergal}
{composer: Robert A. Schumann}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 541}
{meta: tune CANONBURY}
{meta: meter L.M.}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Lord, [G]speak [F#dim]to [Em]me, [Am]that [D7]I may speak
[G/B]in [C]living [G/B]echoes [D]of [Am]thy [D]tone;
[D]as [G]thou [Bm]has [Em]sought, [Am]so [D7]let me seek
[G/B]thine [C]erring [G/B]children [C]lost [G/D]and [D]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]O [G]lead [F#dim]me, [Em]Lord, [Am]that [D7]I may lead
[G/B]the wandering and [A/C#]the wavering [D]feet;
[D]O [G]feed [Bm]me, [Em]Lord, [Am]that [D7]I may feed
[G/B]thy hungering ones [C]with [G/D]manna sweet.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]O [G]strengthen [Em]me, [Am]that while [D7]I stand
[G/B]firm [C]on [D7/A]the [G/B]rock, [A/C#]and [D]strong [Am]in [D]thee,
[D]I [G]may [Bm]stretch [Em]out [Am]a [D7]loving land
[G/B]to [C]wrestlers [G/B]with [C]the [G/D]troubled [D]sea.
{end_of_verse}
